<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pribina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 861</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pribina was a Slavic prince who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nitra">Nitra</a> in the early 9th century until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mojmir-i">Mojmír I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> expelled him around 833. He entered Frankish service, and around 839 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> granted him lands in Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, where he built a fortified seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zalavar">Mosapurc</a>, now Zalavár, and founded churches consecrated by the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a>. He was killed fighting the Moravians in 861 and was succeeded by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kocel">Kocel</a>.</p></div>
